    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d804">

                <pb facs="1090" n="984" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg984"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) City of Flint/1: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-23T23:00:00-05:00">October 23,
                            1939—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>202. Tass<anchor n="71" xml:id="d804-f1"/> despatch from Moscow reports American
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">City of Flint</hi> has arrived at Kola Bay
                    (other news agencies say Murmansk) <pb facs="1091" n="985" xml:id="pg985"/> with
                    German Prize crew on board and that “crew” has been interned.<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d804-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Telegraph urgently such information as you can immediately obtain from Soviet
                    authorities particularly whether it is the American crew or the German prize
                    crew which has been interned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d804-f1" n="71" xml:id="d804-f1-content">
                <p>Telegraph Agency of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d804-f2" n="72" xml:id="d804-f2-content">
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">City of Flint</hi> was an American steamer of the
                    United States Maritime Commission operated by the United States Lines Company,
                    Captain Joseph A. Gainard, master. The
                    ship had left Philadelphia on September 20, 1939, and New York on October 3,
                    with a mixed cargo for England and Europe. During the afternoon of October 9, it
                    had been stopped by the German pocket battleship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Deutschland</hi>, and a German prize crew placed on board, as a portion of
                    the cargo was deemed to be contraband. The ship had stopped at Tromsø, Norway,
                    on October 21 for supplies. From there, instead of proceeding to a German port
                    as expected, it next appeared at the Soviet port of Murmansk.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
